From 45f975a7eae702862c8010162adbee9264b90c0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creitin Gameplays <clton999@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] diag: capture initcall hangs through ramoops and an
 early AON watchdog

The panel rendering became less readable after the glyph scaling change, so
this diagnostic image disables the framebuffer text console. Instead,
init/main.c emits one pr_emerg breadcrumb before each do_basic_setup step and
before each initcall. The 32 KiB ramoops console ring is registered by
postcore_initcall and should retain the final breadcrumb across a warm reset.
The image cmdline adds ignore_loglevel so console=null/loglevel=1 cannot
filter those messages.

For DIAG_WDT_EARLY_INIT builds, register the Spreadtrum watchdog platform
driver at subsys_initcall rather than device_initcall. This is after OF clock
setup and before device initcalls such as KVM, and the existing DIAG probe
arms the hardware watchdog using the driver's clock setup. The late-initcall
feeder takes over in a continuing boot. A pre-feeder hang should now cause a
warm hardware reset and preserve ramoops, avoiding a manual cold power cycle.

Build verified with scripts/host/stage_build.sh 0 0 0 0 0; packed 64 MiB
image boot_ramlog.img has intact ARMd Image header and cmdline token
ignore_loglevel. Device test is pending.
